---
import Layout from "../../components/Layout.astro";
import Ornament from "../../components/Ornament.astro";
import { withBase, BRANCHES } from "../../lib/site.js";
import { grailVersions, voiceById } from "../../lib/portal-data.js";

const v = grailVersions();
const cols = v.columns.map((c) => ({ ...c, voiceRec: voiceById(c.voice) }));
---

<Layout
  title="Six Grails"
  description="The Grail compared across every version that disagrees: what it is, who may approach it, what heals the wound, how you fail, and what it costs."
  current="/grail"
>
  <div class="page-head">
    <span class="rubric">The Grail</span>
    <h1>Six Grails, side by side</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      The same word, six incompatible objects. Read down a column for one author&rsquo;s coherent
      position; read across a row to see the tradition contradicting itself.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="data grail-table">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th scope="col" class="grail-table__corner"></th>
          {cols.map((c) => (
            <th scope="col" data-branch={c.voiceRec?.branch ?? undefined}>
              <a href={withBase(`/library/${c.voice}/`)}>{c.label}</a>
              <span class="grail-table__when">{c.when}</span>
            </th>
          ))}
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {v.rows.map((r) => (
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">{r.label}</th>
            {cols.map((c) => (
              <td data-branch={c.voiceRec?.branch ?? undefined}>{c[r.key]}</td>
            ))}
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <Ornament />

  <section class="narrow narrow--flush">
    <span class="rubric">The sharpest contradiction</span>
    <h2>Pity against purity</h2>
    <p>
      Look at the row marked <em>what heals the wound</em>. Wolfram: one question, asked out of
      pity. The <em>Queste</em>: nothing &mdash; it judges rather than heals.
    </p>
    <p>
      These two books were written within about a decade of each other, by men working from the same
      unfinished French poem, and they disagree about the most basic thing it is possible to
      disagree about: whether the sacred is something that comes to meet a damaged person, or
      something a damaged person is disqualified from.
    </p>
    <p>
      The row marked <em>how you fail</em> is worth the same attention, and it has a page of its
      own: <a href={withBase("/grail/unasked-question/")}>the unasked question</a> follows a single
      scene through four traditions and shows the fault being rewritten while the events stay
      identical.
    </p>
    <p>
      There is no synthesis available. That is not a defect in the record. It is what the Matter of
      Britain <em>is</em> &mdash; five centuries of writers arguing, in narrative, about questions
      nobody has settled since.
    </p>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .grail-table { font-size: 0.9rem; }
  .grail-table thead th {
    text-transform: none;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    color: var(--branch-ink);
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--branch);
    vertical-align: bottom;
    min-width: 9rem;
  }
  .grail-table thead th a { color: inherit; text-decoration: none; }
  .grail-table thead th a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
  .grail-table__when {
    display: block;
    font-family: var(--font-ui);
    font-size: 0.68rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    color: var(--ink-faint);
    margin-top: 0.2em;
    font-weight: 400;
  }
  .grail-table tbody th {
    text-align: left;
    font-family: var(--font-rubric);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    color: var(--ink);
    text-transform: none;
    white-space: nowrap;
    border-right: 1px solid var(--line-strong);
    background: var(--paper-sunk);
    position: sticky;
    left: 0;
  }
  .grail-table td { line-height: 1.45; }
  .grail-table tbody tr:hover td { background: var(--branch-wash); }
  .grail-table__corner { background: var(--paper-sunk); }
</style>
